# Normalize all text files to LF *in the repository*.
#
# The working tree legitimately mixes CRLF and LF (core.autocrlf=true on Windows,
# LF from editors elsewhere). Since git normalizes text on commit either way, this
# rule changes nothing about the stored history - it just makes the normalization
# explicit and stops new files from being committed with mixed line endings.
#
# Deliberately no `eol=crlf`: that would renormalize the ~34 text files that are
# currently LF on disk and produce a large line-ending-only diff.
* text=auto

# Windows launchers must keep CRLF in the working tree to stay runnable.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Binary assets: never diff, never merge.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.gif binary
*.jar binary
*.apk binary
*.keystore binary
*.jks binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.zip binary
